  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "La libreta del equipo",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"La libreta del equipo\"**\n\nAcuérdalo should feel like a notebook the whole team shares. The paper is warm and calm (Lino Cálido), the ink is a single indigo, and soft color tabs mark what state each thing is in. It is an Operate tool for a small agency team, so the notebook organizes work rather than decorating it. Every surface answers \"what's pending, what's overdue, what's coming up\" before it adds any personality.\n\nThe character is **friendly and precise**. Corners are soft, filters are rounded pills, and shadows are barely there. Nothing raises its voice except the primary action and anything that has gone overdue. The warmth comes from small, repeated decisions: avatars with a stable color per person, tinted columns by status, a drawn icon next to every label, and empty states that invite action instead of leaving a gap.\n\nDensity is medium. Desktop is for planning (kanban, week view), the phone is for acting (list, agenda, floating button). The system gets simpler on mobile; it doesn't just shrink.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm stone background with white paper surfaces and a single indigo accent.",
      "Color carries meaning (status, priority, urgency, person), never decoration.",
      "One icon family (lucide, 16px, 1.5 stroke) next to every label in navigation, filters and states.",
      "Pills and segmented controls for filtering and switching views; avatars with a color per person.",
      "Inter at small sizes, tabular numerals for dates and counters."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Ink Rule",
        "body": "Indigo is the only brand color. If an element is indigo, it is either the primary action or something active or current. It is never decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Color Alone Rule",
